    "sha": "f65be5ca15d58ad595cbde3f78f73af23b3690dc",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKGY2NWJlNWNhMTVkNThhZDU5NWNiZGUzZjc4ZjczYWYyM2IzNjkwZGM",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mikekinney@Mikes-MacBook-Pro.local",
        "date": "2026-11-10T21:59:59Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mikekinney@Mikes-MacBook-Pro.local",
        "date": "2026-11-10T21:59:59Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(wcs): anchor the WCS on a picked circle's centre; tidy the WCS page\n\nA shared pick primitive, app::pick::circle (circle_centre /\ncircle_of_edge / circle_of_run): an edge pick resolves to its run and,\nwhen every vertex lies on one planar circle within the feature graph's\narc tolerance, returns centre, axis and radius; a straight edge, a run\ntoo short to call round, a non-circular curve, a face or a vertex is\nrefused by name (CircleRefusal), never guessed.\n\nSetWcsAtCircleCentre wraps SetWcsOrigin at that centre (one undo step,\nundo restores the previous origin) and the MCP tool\nset_wcs_circle_centre runs it. The WCS page gains \"Circle centre\" under\nAnchor on (pick a circular edge; the page states the circle), and is\nlaid out in three sections: a label | field grid, quarter turns as equal\nbuttons filling the pane, and the anchor points as a centred 3x3 compass\nof equal cells.\n\nThe page moved out of pages.rs (egui_app/wcs_page.rs) and the SetWcs\ndispatch arm out of state.rs (state_wcs.rs), so no file past 400 lines\ngrew.\n\nFixes #739\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
